{"result":[{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["kalecki.m"],"name":"Kalecki, M."}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":"szymiczek.kazimierz","reviewer_id":"1709","name":"Kazimierz Szymiczek","sign":"Kazimierz Szymiczek (Katowice)"},"text":"An inductive proof of the following theorem is given. Let \\(m\\) run over natural numbers which have \\(\\Omega\\) prime factors. If \\(m\\) has \\(\\omega\\) distinct prime factors, then between \\(m\\) and \\(2m\\) there are at least \\(\\omega\\) numbers having \\(\\Omega\\) prime factors. If \\(\\Omega=1\\) and \\(p_r\\) is the \\(r\\)-th prime, we get \\(p_{r+1} < 2p_r\\).","contribution_type":"review"}],"id":3245575,"identifier":"0153.06502","keywords":["generalization of Bertrand's postulate"],"language":{"languages":["Polish"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[],"msc":[{"code":"11A41","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Primes"}],"references":[],"source":{"book":[],"pages":"219-220","series":[{"acronym":null,"issn":[{"number":"0373-8302","type":"print"}],"issue":null,"issue_id":135582,"parallel_title":"Annales Societatis Mathematicae Polonae. Seria II. Wiadomości Matematyczne","part":null,"publisher":"Polskie Towarzystwo Matematycne, Warszawa","series_id":857,"short_title":"Rocz. Pol. Tow. Mat., Ser. II, Wiad. Mat.","title":"Roczniki Polskiego Towarzystwa Matematycznego. Seria II. Wiadomości Matematyczne","volume":"9","year":"1967"}],"source":"Rocz. Pol. Tow. Mat., Ser. II, Wiad. Mat. 9, 219-220 (1967)."},"states":[["s","item with single author"]],"title":{"addition":null,"original":"Verallgemeinerung des Bertrandschen Postulats","subtitle":null,"title":"Generalization of Bertrand's postulate"},"year":"1967","zbmath_url":"https://zbmath.org/3245575"},{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"0","codes":["hauchecorne.bertrand"],"name":"Hauchecorne, Bertrand"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"2026-08-07T15:45:23Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":"lemmermeyer.franz","reviewer_id":"7864","name":"Franz Lemmermeyer","sign":"Franz Lemmermeyer (Jagstzell)"},"text":"This volume's great theorem is Bertrand's postulate that for each integer \\(n > 2\\) there is always a prime number \\(p\\) with \\(n < p < 2n\\). The first proofs were given by Chebyshev, Landau and Ramanujan; today, the clever proof by \\textit{P. Erdős} [Acta Litt. Sci. Szeged 5, 194--198 (1932; JFM 58.0154.04)] using ideas of \\textit{E. Landau} [Vorlesungen über Zahlentheorie. I: Aus der elementaren und additiven Zahlentheorie. II: Aus der analytischen und geometrischen Zahlentheorie. III: Aus der algebraischen Zahlentheorie und über die Fermatsche Vermutung Leipzig: S. Hirzel (1927; JFM 53.0123.17)] and the central binomial coefficients is well known to every number theorist (see [\\textit{M. Aigner} and \\textit{G. M. Ziegler}, Proofs from THE BOOK. Including illustrations by Karl H. Hofmann. Revised and enlarged 6th edition. Berlin: Springer (2018; Zbl 1392.00001)]).","contribution_type":"review"}],"id":8237174,"identifier":null,"keywords":["Bertrand's postulate","binomial coefficients"],"language":{"languages":["French"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[],"msc":[{"code":"11N05","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Distribution of primes"}],"references":[],"source":{"book":[],"pages":"4-6","series":[{"acronym":null,"issn":[{"number":"1142-2785","type":"print"},{"number":"1760-4826","type":"electronic"}],"issue":null,"issue_id":529468,"parallel_title":null,"part":null,"publisher":"Quadrature, Paris","series_id":2179,"short_title":"Quadrature","title":"Quadrature","volume":"136","year":"2025"}],"source":"Quadratu